 Safe Browsing: Recognizing Secure Websites
One of the first practical lessons in internet usage is learning to identify secure websites.
Users should look for "HTTPS" in the address bar and a padlock icon, which indicate that the connection between their browser and the website is encrypted. 
This is especially critical when entering sensitive information like passwords or credit card details. Understanding that "HTTP"
without the "S" is unencrypted helps users avoid phishing sites and protects them from data interception.
This simple habit is a cornerstone of personal cybersecurity.
